Today is Wednesday, and I am walking home in the evening.
On the way, I stop at the vegetable market.
I buy fresh vegetables here every week.
The vendor smiles on seeing me.
He knows my favourite vegetables.
I go to my familiar vegetable vendor.
"Namaste!"
"Are the tomatoes fresh today?" I ask him.
He smiles and says, "Yes madam, they are very fresh."
"Please give me one kilo of tomatoes," I say.
The vendor puts the tomatoes in a small box.
"Do you need spinach today?" he asks.
"Yes, I also need spinach and potatoes," I say.
He weighs all the vegetables.
"What is the total price?" I ask.
"It is two hundred rupees," the vendor replies.
I give him the money.
He gives me the receipt and the vegetables.
I carefully put the vegetables in my bag.
I say thank you to him and walk towards home.
This quiet routine makes me very happy.
